A||||3||walsh2001||Fiero Memorial:||||10||
Z||000000||walsh2001||10-12-2001||09:43 AM||||I wrote this poem the other day for my English class... It is a memorial to my 84' coupe:<P>ODE TO A CAR<P>Drip, Drip, Drip,<BR>The Fiero sits.<BR>The life oil flowing,<BR>Ebbing, pooling, shiny…<BR>Rainbow sheen reflected on gray concrete.<P>Splash, flood, rupture,<BR>Heater pipes split.<BR>Coolant seeping, then gushing,<BR>Pouring, spreading, steaming…<BR>Clear green fluid lapping at my feet.<P>Chatter, Rumble, Crack,<BR>Clutch plate shatters.<BR>Shifter slack, gears useless,<BR>Grinding, screaming, frustration…<BR>Anger forming deep down inside me.<P>“Cha-ching”, print, groan,<BR>Cash register chirps.<BR>Expenses rising rapidly,<BR>Rising, inflating, multiplying…<P>	…Fiero For Sale.<P>…. Jason Walsh<P>...... I ordered new KYB shocks and struts for my 87 GT; are they an easy install? Any recomendations? Also will a new steering dampner (the little shock on the rack) have any noticeable effect?<P><P>------------------<BR>'87 Fiero GT ... Cherry Red||||reg||10
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||10-12-2001||06:21 PM||||Hey Jason!<BR>I like!<BR>The shocks are easy, but you may want to rent spring comressors from u-rent it or whom ever...<BR>crash...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-13-2001||03:53 PM||||I built my own set of spring compressors..<P>WIll post pics if anyones interested..<P>took 10 minutes and $7. canadian worth of hardware to make<P>||||reg||1
